## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design distributed workflows across microservices with CQRS/ES, ensuring tenant isolation, idempotency, and reliable message delivery.

## Key Concepts
- Long-running sagas with compensating transactions for rollback scenarios
- CQRS and Event Sourcing with versioned events for auditability and replay
- Outbox pattern ensuring at-least-once delivery
- Idempotency via correlationId and deduplication checks
- Per-tenant read models maintaining data isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Event-to-command mapping with deduplication
function handleEvent(evt, state) {
  if (state.processed?.includes(evt.id)) return;

  const cmd = mapEventToCommand(evt);
  enqueueToOutbox(cmd);
  state.processed = [...(state.processed || []), evt.id];
}

// Saga orchestration with compensation
async function executeOnboardSaga(tenantId, correlationId) {
  try {
    await TenantAuth.create(tenantId, correlationId);
    await Billing.setupQuota(tenantId, correlationId);
    await DataIngestion.provision(tenantId, correlationId);
    await Analytics.initialize(tenantId, correlationId);
  } catch (error) {
    await compensateSaga(tenantId, correlationId);
  }
}

async function compensateSaga(tenantId, correlationId) {
  await Analytics.deprovision(tenantId, correlationId);
  await DataIngestion.stop(tenantId, correlationId);
  await Billing.revertQuota(tenantId, correlationId);
  await TenantAuth.delete(tenantId, correlationId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the candidate's ability to handle cross-service compensation, drift recovery, and per-tenant isolation in a Saga-driven, event-sourced architecture.

## Key Concepts
- **Saga Orchestration**: Coordinating distributed transactions with compensating actions
- **CQRS & Event Sourcing**: Managing read/write separation and handling state drift
- **Outbox Pattern**: Ensuring reliable event publication for replay after failures
- **Idempotency**: Preventing duplicate processing with tenant-scoped keys
- **Per-Tenant Thresholds**: Custom anomaly handling per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Orchestrator skeleton
class RefundOrchestrator {
  constructor(outboxStore, tenantConfig) {
    this.outbox = outboxStore;
    this.config = tenantConfig;
  }

  async start(orderId, tenantId) {
    const tenant = this.config.get(tenantId);
    await this.outbox.append({
      type: 'RefundCommand',
      orderId,
      tenantId,
      maxRetries: tenant.maxRefundRetries,
      timeoutMs: tenant.refundTimeoutMs
    });
  }

  async onRefundResult(evt) {
    if (evt.status === 'success') {
      await this.completeOrder(evt.orderId, evt.tenantId);
    } else {
      await this.triggerCompensation(evt.orderId, evt.tenantId);
    }
  }

  async triggerCompensation(orderId, tenantId) {
    const tenant = this.config.get(tenantId);
    if (tenant.refundRetries >= tenant.maxRefundRetries) {
      await this.outbox.append({
        type: 'CompensatingTransaction',
        orderId,
        tenantId,
        action: 'VOID_PAYMENT'
      });
    }
  }
}
```
